    "turn_idx": 89,
    "turn_text": "It's really interesting to hear all of all of that insight and particularly in a year that has been uncertain for for just so so many people it is refreshing for me to hear that that there is work getting done that there's progress being made. Senator you know I guess I'll I'll take a little bit of step back if you think about you mentioned you are at our annual meeting last year and in December of 2019 and I am pleased to tell you that the Board of Directors did vote last week to go ahead and have our annual meeting that we're going to make some modifications. We're going to kind of condense it down and try to do social distancing and take all those precautions. But hopefully we will be able to see you down there in December. But if you think about 2019, You know, we came through 2019 and at our annual meeting, everybody just said, well, let's get on to 2020. Things have got to get better than they were in 2019. And 2019 was a hard year for a lot of people, particularly along. the Missouri and Mississippi rivers. I know that you have been a strong player in the Senate's discussion around water infrastructure projects. So as we as we think back it it seems like it's been a little bit longer than a couple years ago but you know as we look back at the devastation we saw what do you think are the some sets being taken to continue that recovery process because that's continued to be ongoing even despite the pandemic.",
